# 3. CORE RULE — VOCABULARY MUST DETERMINE THE SCENE

The existing implementation appears to sometimes display images that do not contain the objects students are asked to identify.

This must be corrected.

**Every Identify scene must be created specifically to represent its intended vocabulary.**

The workflow must be:

1. Select the target vocabulary.
2. Verify the intended meaning of each word.
3. Determine whether the words can naturally appear together.
4. Design a suitable visual scene.
5. Generate or select a matching image.
6. Verify the actual visible objects.
7. Locate the objects within the image.
8. Generate accurate object annotations.
9. Validate scene quality.
10. Preview the completed exercise.
11. Approve the scene for publication.

Do not select an unrelated image and assign vocabulary to arbitrary areas.

Do not assume that an object exists merely because it appeared in an image-generation prompt.

The final rendered image must be visually inspected or otherwise reliably verified.

